// Strangers (non-regular guests): what they look like, how Karolina describes them until she
// knows them, and the first names they tell her. Read by `src/sim/names.rs` (compiled in).
//
// * `female` / `male`: first names — [Latin (cs, en), Cyrillic (uk), optional Russian spelling].
//   Names of regulars, story staff and the cast are left out on purpose (Hana, Vera, Bára, Ema…).
// * `styles`: per guest archetype (`guests.ron` id): the share of women, of elderly guests, the
//   tops and extras they wear (weights) and whole-phrase descriptions (`phrases`). A phrase may
//   need a visible feature (`needs: Extra(FlatCap)` / `Top(Coat)`); it is only used when the
//   guest really wears it. Generic phrases for every extra / top / elderly guest exist on top.
//   Texts: `stranger.<phrase>.<f|m>` and `stranger.<phrase>.<f|m>.short` in
//   `assets/i18n/src/guest_names.tr`.
// * Earrings and hair clips are only ever drawn on women; elderly guests wear calm extras.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
(
    female: [
        ["Tereza", "Тереза"], ["Klára", "Клара"], ["Lenka", "Ленка"], ["Markéta", "Маркета"],
        ["Eliška", "Елішка", "Элишка"], ["Zuzana", "Зузана"], ["Petra", "Петра"],
